# XSH getsid()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.

assertion  XSH.getsid.001
anchor     functions/getsid.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/getsid.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2008
says       In a session started by c1 (setsid()), where c2 leads a group of
           its own and c3 stays in c1's group, c2's getsid() of c1, c2 and
           c3 each returns c1; the test process, in another session, gets
           c1 or EPERM from getsid(c2).
note       Whether a process in another session may be asked is left to
           the implementation.
test       t/001-session.c

assertion  XSH.getsid.002
anchor     functions/getsid.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2008
says       getsid(0) in c2 (leader of its own group in c1's session)
           returns c1.
test       t/002-zero.c

assertion  XSH.getsid.003
anchor     functions/getsid.html#ERRORS/ESRCH
anchor     functions/getsid.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2008
says       getsid() of the ID of a child whose status has been collected
           (and which no process has reused) returns -1 with ESRCH.
test       t/003-esrch.c
